{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:76f79d0545e98c14","name":"Atmospheric Thrusters","source":{"id":"source:reference-76f79d0545e98c14","title":"Atmospheric Thrusters","revision":15994,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:53:30Z","sha256":"2fcf7d0dfea1fb02ae53deac6a73e52696deb21fca0c8c5622c9d1ac6bf67e12","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15994","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Atmospheric%20Thrusters&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-76f79d0545e98c14","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ATMOSPHERIC THRUSTERS\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EP\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AVAILABILITY\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE RESTRICTION\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Standard\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Common\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal or Smaller\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2,000 (Base)\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Advanced\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Common\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gargantuan or Smaller\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5,000 (Base)\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Atmospheric Thrusters increase a Starship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," when the ship is flying in the atmosphere of a planet. Any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," able to operate in an atmosphere has some engine system designed for air flight, normally a combination of repulsorlifts and ion engines. Atmospheric Thrusters are an augmentation of these base systems, designed to make the Starship more competitive with a dedicated ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Standard Atmospheric Thrusters increase a Starship's maximum velocity and fly ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," by 10%, while Advanced Atmospheric Thrusters increase these by 25% (rounded down to the nearest square of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," and 10 km/h). Thus, an ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing"}," with Standard Atmospheric Thrusters has a maximum velocity of 1,150 km/h and a fly ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," of 17 squares at ",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Character_Scale"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Atmospheric Thrusters have no effect on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," movement.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
